2 = 24 - 2 = 22","Third term = 22 * 3 - 2 = 64","Fourth term = 64 * 3 - 2 = 190","Fifth Term = 190 * 3 - 2 = 568","Sixth Term = 568 * 3 - 2 = 1704 - 2 = 1702"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e16fa20b9bf207ccab29ff","text":["What will come at the place of question mark ? 8, 22, 64, 190, 568, ?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" 1702 ","image":"","_id":"65e16fa20b9bf207ccab2a00"},{"text":"7767 ","image":"","_id":"65e16fa20b9bf207ccab2a01"},{"text":" 6992 ","image":"","_id":"65e16fa20b9bf207ccab2a02"},{"text":"6913","image":"","_id":"65e16fa20b9bf207ccab2a03"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T06:03:14.310Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T06:03:14.310Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["This is a simple alternating addition and subtraction series. In the first pattern, 3 is added; in the second, 2 is subtracted.","Alternate Solution :","Above Series contains two sub series in it","Series 1st = 7, 8, 9, 10","Series 2nd = 10, 11, 12","","Note : Both sub series is in ascending order. Next number is greater by 1 from the previous one."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e1709c0b9bf207ccab2b5e","text":["7, 10, 8, 11, 9, 12, ... What number should come next?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"7","image":"","_id":"65e1709c0b9bf207ccab2b5f"},{"text":"10","image":"","_id":"65e1709c0b9bf207ccab2b60"},{"text":"12","image":"","_id":"65e1709c0b9bf207ccab2b61"},{"text":"13","image":"","_id":"65e1709c0b9bf207ccab2b62"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T06:07:24.089Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T06:07:24.089Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["This is a simple division series; each number is one-half of the previous number.","In other terms to say, the number is divided by 2 successively to get the next result.","4/2 = 2","2/2 = 1","1/2 = 1/2","1/2/2 = 1/4","1/4/2 = 1/8 and so on."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e1704a0b9bf207ccab2ae5","text":["2, 1, 1/2, 1/4, . . . . . . What number should come next?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" 1/3 ","image":"","_id":"65e1704a0b9bf207ccab2ae6"},{"text":" 1/8  ","image":"","_id":"65e1704a0b9bf207ccab2ae7"},{"text":"2/8","image":"","_id":"65e1704a0b9bf207ccab2ae8"},{"text":"1/16","image":"","_id":"65e1704a0b9bf207ccab2ae9"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T06:06:02.062Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T06:06:02.062Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["First Term = 5760.","","Second term = 5760 /2 = 2880.","","Third Term = 2880/3 = 960.","","Fourth term = 960/4 = 240.","","Fifth term = 240/5 = 48.","","So, Required term = 48/6 = 8."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e16feb0b9bf207ccab2a70","text":["What will come at the place of question mark ? 5760,2880,960, 240, 48, ?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"6","image":"","_id":"65e16feb0b9bf207ccab2a71"},{"text":"8","image":"","_id":"65e16feb0b9bf207ccab2a72"},{"text":"12","image":"","_id":"65e16feb0b9bf207ccab2a73"},{"text":"16","image":"","_id":"65e16feb0b9bf207ccab2a74"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T06:04:27.072Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T06:04:27.072Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["This is an alternating number subtraction series. First, 2 is subtracted, then 4, then 2, and so on."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e1711c0b9bf207ccab2bdf","text":["36, 34, 30, 28, 24, ... What number should come next?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"20","image":"","_id":"65e1711c0b9bf207ccab2be0"},{"text":"22","image":"","_id":"65e1711c0b9bf207ccab2be1"},{"text":"23","image":"","_id":"65e1711c0b9bf207ccab2be2"},{"text":"26","image":"","_id":"65e1711c0b9bf207ccab2be3"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T06:09:32.993Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T06:09:32.993Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The second and forth letters in the series, L and A, are static. The first and third letters consist of an alphabetical order beginning with the letter E."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690ebb5958f537157013951","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","ELFA, GLHA, ILJA, _____, MLNA"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"OLPA","image":"","_id":"6690ebb5958f537157013952"},{"text":" KLMA","image":"","_id":"6690ebb5958f537157013953"},{"text":" LLMA","image":"","_id":"6690ebb5958f537157013954"},{"text":" KLLA","image":"","_id":"6690ebb5958f537157013955"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T08:39:17.114Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T08:39:17.114Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["There are three series to look for here. The first letters are alphabetical in reverse: Z, Y, X, W, V. The second letters are in alphabetical order, beginning with A. The number series is as follows: 5, 4, 6, 3, 7."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690ec60958f537157017f75","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","","$ZA_5$, $Y4_B$, $XC_6$, $W_3$D, _____"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$E_7V$","image":"","_id":"6690ec60958f537157017f76"},{"text":"$V_2E$","image":"","_id":"6690ec60958f537157017f77"},{"text":"$VE_5$","image":"","_id":"6690ec60958f537157017f78"},{"text":"$VE_7$","image":"","_id":"6690ec60958f537157017f79"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T08:42:08.683Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T08:42:08.683Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In this series, the letters remain the same: DEF.","","The subscript numbers follow this series:","","111, 112, 122, 222, 223, 233, 333, ..."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690ecf3958f53715701a996","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","DEF, $DEF_2$, $DE_2F_2$, _____, $D_2E_2F_3$"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$DEF_3$","image":"","_id":"6690ecf3958f53715701a997"},{"text":"$D_3EF_3$","image":"","_id":"6690ecf3958f53715701a998"},{"text":"$D_2E_3F$","image":"","_id":"6690ecf3958f53715701a999"},{"text":"$D_2E_2F_2$","image":"","_id":"6690ecf3958f53715701a99a"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T08:44:35.156Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T08:44:35.156Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["There are two alphabetical series here. The first series is with the first letters only: STUVW. The second series involves the remaining letters: CD, EF, GH, IJ, KL."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f3e2958f53715703c465","text":["SCD, TEF, UGH, ____, WKL",""],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"CMN","image":"","_id":"6690f3e2958f53715703c466"},{"text":"UJI","image":"","_id":"6690f3e2958f53715703c467"},{"text":" VIJ","image":"","_id":"6690f3e2958f53715703c468"},{"text":" IJT","image":"","_id":"6690f3e2958f53715703c469"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:14:10.896Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:14:10.896Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Because the letters are the same, concentrate on the number series, which is a simple 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 series, and follows each letter in order.",""],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f478958f53715703c46b","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","$B_2CD$, _____, $BCD_4$, $B_5CD$, $BC_6D$"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" $B_2C_2D$","image":"","_id":"6690f478958f53715703c46c"},{"text":" $BC_3D$","image":"","_id":"6690f478958f53715703c46d"},{"text":"$B_2C_3D$","image":"","_id":"6690f478958f53715703c46e"},{"text":"$BCD_7$","image":"","_id":"6690f478958f53715703c46f"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:16:40.662Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:16:40.662Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The first letters are in alphabetical order with a letter skipped in between each segment: C, E, G, I, K. The second and third letters are repeated; they are also in order with a skipped letter: M, O, Q, S, U."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f4f7958f53715703c500","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","CMM, EOO, GQQ, _____, KUU"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"GRR","image":"","_id":"6690f4f7958f53715703c501"},{"text":"GSS","image":"","_id":"6690f4f7958f53715703c502"},{"text":"ISS","image":"","_id":"6690f4f7958f53715703c503"},{"text":"ITT","image":"","_id":"6690f4f7958f53715703c504"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:18:47.464Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:18:47.464Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["This is an alternating series in alphabetical order. The middle letters follow the order ABCDE. The first and third letters are alphabetical beginning with J. The third letter is repeated as a first letter in each subsequent three-letter segment."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f58b958f53715703c5cf","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","JAK, KBL, LCM, MDN, _____"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"OEP","image":"","_id":"6690f58b958f53715703c5d0"},{"text":" NEO","image":"","_id":"6690f58b958f53715703c5d1"},{"text":" MEN","image":"","_id":"6690f58b958f53715703c5d2"},{"text":"PFQ","image":"","_id":"6690f58b958f53715703c5d3"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:21:15.636Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:21:15.636Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The series is yxxy/yxxy/yxxy/yxxy. Thus, the pattern 'yxxy' is repeated."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f6b1958f53715703c6eb","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","_ xx _ yx _ yy _ xy _ xxy"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"xxxyy","image":"","_id":"6690f6b1958f53715703c6ec"},{"text":"yxyxy","image":"","_id":"6690f6b1958f53715703c6ed"},{"text":"yyxxy","image":"","_id":"6690f6b1958f53715703c6ee"},{"text":"yyyxx","image":"","_id":"6690f6b1958f53715703c6ef"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:26:09.385Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:26:09.385Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The series is xyxzpx/xyxzpx/xyxzpx/xyxzpx. Thus, the pattern ' xyxzpx' is repeated."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f73a958f53715703c792","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","xy _ z _ xxyx _ px _ yxzpx _ yxzpx"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" xpzxx","image":"","_id":"6690f73a958f53715703c793"},{"text":"yxyzx","image":"","_id":"6690f73a958f53715703c794"},{"text":"yxzpx","image":"","_id":"6690f73a958f53715703c795"},{"text":" zyxpy","image":"","_id":"6690f73a958f53715703c796"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:28:26.239Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:28:26.239Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["First letter in every group is in reverse alphabetical order i.e. SRQPON. The middle letter is in alphabetical order i.e ABCDEF and the last letter has pairs, BB, DD & FF."],"images":[]},"_id":"6690f7a5958f53715703c79e","text":["Fill the blank in the middle of the series or end of the series.","SAB,_____, QCD, PDD, OEF, NFF"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"CBT","image":"","_id":"6690f7a5958f53715703c79f"},{"text":"ABR","image":"","_id":"6690f7a5958f53715703c7a0"},{"text":"BCT","image":"","_id":"6690f7a5958f53715703c7a1"},{"text":"RBB","image":"","_id":"6690f7a5958f53715703c7a2"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-07-12T09:30:13.863Z","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T09:30:13.863Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["It is a simple division series in which each number is one-half of the previous number. We can also say that each number is divided by 2 to arrive at the next number;","","On dividing 48 by 2, we get 24","","On dividing 24 by 2, we get 12","","So, on dividing 12 by 2, we will get 6 (option B)."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a39c6ffffda09635050d","text":["Which number should come next in the series, 48, 24, 12, ......?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"8","image":"","_id":"6728a39c6ffffda09635050e"},{"text":"6","image":"","_id":"6728a39c6ffffda09635050f"},{"text":"4","image":"","_id":"6728a39c6ffffda096350510"},{"text":"2","image":"","_id":"6728a39c6ffffda096350511"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:36:12.134Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:36:12.134Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["We can see that it is an alternating number subtraction series; first 2 is subtracted then 4 is subtracted and then 2 is subtracted again and so on;","","46 - 2 = 44","","44 - 4 = 40","","40 - 2 = 38","","38 - 4 = 34","","34 - 2 = 32 (option C)"],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a3c46ffffda096350513","text":["Look at the series, 46, 44, 40, 38, 34, _, which number should come next?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"30","image":"","_id":"6728a3c46ffffda096350514"},{"text":"36","image":"","_id":"6728a3c46ffffda096350515"},{"text":"32","image":"","_id":"6728a3c46ffffda096350516"},{"text":"31","image":"","_id":"6728a3c46ffffda096350517"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:36:52.491Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:36:52.491Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In this series, the difference between the consecutive numbers increases by 2;","","7 - 4 = 3","12 - 7 = 5","19 - 12 = 7","","Therefore, the next number would be 19 + 9 = 28 (option A)"],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a3e76ffffda096350519","text":["Which number would fill the empty space in the series; 4, 7, 12, 19, _, 39?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"28","image":"","_id":"6728a3e76ffffda09635051a"},{"text":"26","image":"","_id":"6728a3e76ffffda09635051b"},{"text":"24","image":"","_id":"6728a3e76ffffda09635051c"},{"text":"22","image":"","_id":"6728a3e76ffffda09635051d"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:37:27.487Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:37:27.487Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In this series, the difference between consecutive numbers is multiplied by 3; 20, 60, 180, 540.","","Therefore, the missing number would be 100 + 180 = 280 (option C)"],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4096ffffda09635051f","text":["Which number would replace the underline mark in the series 20, 40, 100, _, 820?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"240","image":"","_id":"6728a4096ffffda096350520"},{"text":"260","image":"","_id":"6728a4096ffffda096350521"},{"text":"280","image":"","_id":"6728a4096ffffda096350522"},{"text":"300","image":"","_id":"6728a4096ffffda096350523"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:38:01.051Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:38:01.051Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["This is a simple addition series in which the number \"15\" is interpolated as every third number. And, except 15, four is added to each number to arrive at the next number."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4326ffffda09635052b","text":["What are the missing numbers in this series, 15, 20, 24, 15, 28, 32 15, _, _, 15?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"37, 41","image":"","_id":"6728a4326ffffda09635052c"},{"text":"36, 40","image":"","_id":"6728a4326ffffda09635052d"},{"text":"38, 42","image":"","_id":"6728a4326ffffda09635052e"},{"text":"40, 44","image":"","_id":"6728a4326ffffda09635052f"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:38:42.686Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:38:42.686Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The series consists of letters in reverse alphabetical order. Therefore, the missing letters are LKJ."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4626ffffda09635060c","text":["RQP, ONM, _, IHG, FED, find the missing letters."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"CDE","image":"","_id":"6728a4626ffffda09635060d"},{"text":"LKI","image":"","_id":"6728a4626ffffda09635060e"},{"text":"LKJ","image":"","_id":"6728a4626ffffda09635060f"},{"text":"BAC","image":"","_id":"6728a4626ffffda096350610"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:39:30.325Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:39:30.325Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The second and fourth letters (K and L) in the series are static. The first and third letters are in alphabetical order starting with the letter C. So, the missing letters are IKJL."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4866ffffda09635061c","text":["CKDL, EKFL, GKHL, _, KKLL, find the missing letters."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"IJKL","image":"","_id":"6728a4866ffffda09635061d"},{"text":"IKJL","image":"","_id":"6728a4866ffffda09635061e"},{"text":"MNOP","image":"","_id":"6728a4866ffffda09635061f"},{"text":"MNPQ","image":"","_id":"6728a4866ffffda096350620"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:40:06.579Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:40:06.579Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The middle letters in this series follow the order ABCDE. The first and third letters are in alphabetical order starting with the letter G."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4a66ffffda0963507ca","text":["Find the missing letters in the series, GAH, IBJ, KCL, MDN, _."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"OEG","image":"","_id":"6728a4a66ffffda0963507cb"},{"text":"OEP","image":"","_id":"6728a4a66ffffda0963507cc"},{"text":"OEB","image":"","_id":"6728a4a66ffffda0963507cd"},{"text":"OEA","image":"","_id":"6728a4a66ffffda0963507ce"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:40:38.661Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:40:38.661Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The first letters of the series are in an alphabetical order in which a letter is skipped between each two letters; B, D, F, H, J. The second and third letters are repeated in each segment, and they are also in alphabetical order with a skipped letter; K, M, O, Q, S. So, the missing letters are HQQ."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4cd6ffffda09635087d","text":["Find the missing letters in the series, BKK, DMM, FOO, _, JSS."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"HLL","image":"","_id":"6728a4cd6ffffda09635087e"},{"text":"HBB","image":"","_id":"6728a4cd6ffffda09635087f"},{"text":"HTT","image":"","_id":"6728a4cd6ffffda096350880"},{"text":"HQQ","image":"","_id":"6728a4cd6ffffda096350881"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:41:17.516Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:41:17.516Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["The series contains vowels in reverse order, U, O, I, E, A. So, the missing letter is E."],"images":[]},"_id":"6728a4fe6ffffda096350883","text":["What is the missing letter in the series, U, O, I, _, A?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Q","image":"","_id":"6728a4fe6ffffda096350884"},{"text":"K","image":"","_id":"6728a4fe6ffffda096350885"},{"text":"F","image":"","_id":"6728a4fe6ffffda096350886"},{"text":"E","image":"","_id":"6728a4fe6ffffda096350887"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"number_alphabet_series","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-04T10:42:06.189Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-04T10:42:06.189Z","__v":0}]